<!--
    Rec 35 (#35-4): the block_structure yield point, the last bypassable pass
    wired onto the general pass-bypass facade (passShouldBypass, #35-4b). Design
    at DD-0006. block_structure is CollapseStructure::collapseAll
    (ActionBlockStructure), which must reduce the control-flow graph all the way
    to a single root before PrintC can emit it. Unlike the other bypassable
    passes it therefore cannot early-return on truncation (that would hand the
    printer a multi-root graph); instead its coarse mode is "collapse with gotos
    instead of structure"  -  once the budget is spent it stops attempting the
    precise structuring rules (proper-if, if-else, while-do, do-while, infloop,
    switch, ifnoexit, casefallthru) and drives the graph to its single root
    through the existing selectGoto/clipExtraRoots goto-injection path, the same
    all-goto "unstructured" rendering the decompiler already emits for genuinely
    unstructurable control flow. So the result is always valid and printable.

    The cooperative budget caps block_structure in block-scan sweeps (its own
    scale: one full collapseInternal pass over every block, the same per-sweep
    scale data_flow and value_analysis use). Because the positional
    `decompilebudget` form is full at its three flow/data_flow/type_inference
    slots, the cap is set by name through `decompilebudgetpass`.

    The first sweep always runs precise (bypass cannot be set before the first
    tick), so a cap of 1 keeps one sweep of real structuring and forces the tail
    goto-only  -  exactly the "keep the structure the budget bought, degrade the
    rest" contract. The block_structure partial-result header is emitted exactly
    once per function (claimDiagnostic), and the function still prints, which is
    the key invariant DD-0006 turns on: a bypassed structuring pass yields a
    valid partial (a printable single-root function), not a broken result.

    condconst1 has several conditionals, so collapseAll needs more than one
    block-scan sweep to structure it; the unbudgeted decompile of the same
    function is exercised by condconst.xml, the flow_analysis-truncation path by
    decompbudget.xml, data_flow by decompbudget_dataflow.xml, type_inference by
    decompbudget_typeinfer.xml and value_analysis by
    decompbudget_valueanalysis.xml.

    The function bytes are condconst1 from condconst.xml.
-->
